WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:03.844
Hi, welcome back to Nagarjuna,

00:00:03.844 --> 00:00:07.170
Arya Nagarjuna, and
this is the tenth class.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:11.522
We're going to talk about
BCINGS PA DANG THAR PA BRTAG PA

00:00:11.522 --> 00:00:13.575
BCINGS PA DANG THAR PA BRTAG PA

00:00:13.575 --> 00:00:16.742
Say BCINGS PA [students repeat], DANG

00:00:16.742 --> 00:00:19.180
THAR PA, BRTAG PA.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.833
What's BRTAG PA?

00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:22.740
[students responding indistinctly]

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.042
In Sanskrit.

00:00:25.171 --> 00:00:28.020
PARĪKṢĀ (PARIKSHA).

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.690
Okay, an investigation
of BCINGS PA and THAR PA.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:37.620
BCINGS PA means bondage, like
being chained up in the jail,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.350
and THAR PA means freedom.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.250
Now we're going to talk

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:46.250
about the emptiness of
being chained into sansara

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:49.960
and the emptiness of getting
free from those chains.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.990
And let's go to the first verse,

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.383
which is really only half a verse,

00:00:56.874 --> 00:00:58.945
and it starts with GAL TE.

00:01:00.352 --> 00:01:03.342
The guy, you know, Nagarjuna

00:01:03.342 --> 00:01:06.584
is asking the other guy,

00:01:08.025 --> 00:01:10.650
"Who goes around in sansara?"

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.580
Who goes around the circle of sansara?

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.980
Who is it that circles
around in sansara, right?

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:18.500
And it's an interesting question.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.130
And by the way, if you don't understand

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:24.405
who it is that circles around in sansara,

00:01:24.405 --> 00:01:29.284
that causes you to circle
around in sansara [laughs].

00:01:29.284 --> 00:01:31.030
So it's kind of a good question.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:34.796
All right, so ,GAL TE
'DU BYED 'KHOR ZHE NA,

00:01:34.796 --> 00:01:38.030
,DE DAG RTAG NA MI 'KHOR TE,

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.436
So GAL TE means, all right,

00:01:40.436 --> 00:01:42.620
Nagarjuna's talking to the other guy,

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:47.060
"So who is it that wanders
around in sansara?"

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.670
And the other guy says 'DU BYED

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:52.610
which is a confusing answer
because 'DU BYED means factors.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.100
And in fact, it's, for example,

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.850
the name for the second
link in the Wheel of Life,

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.390
which is fresh karma,

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:00.360
and it has nothing to do with that here.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.692
Here it means PHUNG PO.

00:02:03.692 --> 00:02:04.942
The body and mind.

00:02:04.942 --> 00:02:06.440
Yeah, I like to call it
body and mind nowadays

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:07.920
because it's just easier.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.450
It's exactly what we call body and mind.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:16.450
So if you say the thing that
circles around in sansara

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:21.260
is the body mind complex, the
body and the mind together,

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.472
'KHOR ZHE NA

00:02:22.472 --> 00:02:25.770
if that's what circles around in sansara,

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:29.000
are you thinking of body and mind

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.840
as something unchanging or changing?

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.150
When you answer me, when I ask you

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:37.730
who is it that travels through sansara,

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:40.070
who is it that goes from birth to birth,

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.380
and you say it's body and mind,

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.810
it's Michael's body and mind,

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:48.510
and then I say, "Well is
that an unchanging thing

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.290
or is that a changing thing?"

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:53.010
And Nagarjuna typically
covers either answer.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:56.700
So the other guy says it's unchanging.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.780
It's an unchanging thing.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.912
Oh! DE DAG RTAG NA MI 'KHOR TE

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:08.300
If the body and mind of
Michael are unchanging,

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:13.600
and by the way, it shades
into permanent, right?

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.410
The way that some people
mistranslate the word.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.150
It shades into permanent.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:22.280
If it's Michael's permanent body and mind

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:25.410
that keep traveling around sansara,

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.084
RTAG NA MI 'KHOR

00:03:27.084 --> 00:03:29.334
then it cannot circle.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.320
- Why?

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.870
- Because it's RTAG PA,
because it's unchanging.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.380
When you circle, you change.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.890
By circling you change.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.770
Circling means you change.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:44.060
You can't travel somewhere
else if you don't change.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:47.460
At least you have to change
where you put your bottom.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.770
Something's going to
change if you're traveling.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:53.070
So therefore, it cannot be Michael,

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:56.280
unchanging Michael's body and mind,

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.600
which goes from birth to birth.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.200
Then the other guy's
going to come back with,

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.420
"Okay, I change my story.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:05.850
It's the body and mind which is changing."

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:09.450
And there's the next verse, yay.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:13.170
And by the way, the
second half of the verse

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.410
gets split again.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.860
So first part of the
second half of the verse is

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.893
,MI RTAG NA YANG 'KHOR MI 'GYUR,

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.700
,MI RTAG NA YANG 'KHOR MI 'GYUR

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:28.700
If you say Michael's body
and mind are changing,

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:33.580
then they can't circle
around sansara either.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.413
- Why?

00:04:34.413 --> 00:04:38.840
- Because they blink out of
existence every millisecond.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.415
Okay? They last:

00:04:41.415 --> 00:04:42.990
@SKAD CIG GIS SKAD CIG GIS ...

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:46.216
Definition of impermanent, changing.

00:04:46.216 --> 00:04:47.368
SKAD CIG GIS SKAD CIG GIS

00:04:47.368 --> 00:04:49.208
Say SKAD CIG GIS SKAD CIG GIS

00:04:49.208 --> 00:04:50.437
[students repeat]

00:04:50.437 --> 00:04:52.669
@SKAD CIG GIS SKAD CIG GIS

00:04:52.669 --> 00:04:55.370
@

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:59.910
It could be a good song,
@SKAD CIG GIS SKAD CIG GIS...

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:02.210
It means that thing which
comes into existence

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:03.826
and goes out of existence

00:05:03.826 --> 00:05:07.184
SKAD CIG -- instant by instant,

00:05:07.184 --> 00:05:09.975
SKAD CIG GIS SKAD CIG GIS

00:05:11.308 --> 00:05:15.266
So how could that have
a sustained circling

00:05:15.266 --> 00:05:18.530
if it's going out of
existence every millisecond?

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:21.090
How can something which
goes out of existence

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:24.500
every millisecond go in a circle?

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:25.970
It's not possible.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.380
- Why?

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:32.380
- Because each millisecond
of Michael's body and mind

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:37.230
is separated from the millisecond
of Michael's body and mind

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.090
just before that, right?

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:41.670
And we're already
talking, we spent so long

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:43.660
talking about SAṂSARGA (SANSARGA),

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:45.763
Christina, SANSARGA.

00:05:45.763 --> 00:05:47.192
- [Christina] Flowing together.

00:05:47.192 --> 00:05:51.908
Yeah, so if Geshe-la's mind body is

00:05:51.908 --> 00:05:54.260
ta da, ta da, ta da

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:57.450
then there's a separation
between each instant,

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:59.670
and then there's no reason why this one

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:02.220
should go to that one
because they never touch.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:05.850
So this one could change
to Tim's body and mind,

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.350
you know, why not?

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:10.463
Because those are not connected either.

00:06:10.463 --> 00:06:13.863
So if Michael's body
and mind go like this,

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:19.390
then why can't Michael's
body and mind go like this

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:21.870
and become Tim the next instant? Why?

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:24.200
There's no reason why it shouldn't be Tim

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:28.030
because Tim's also
disconnected from Geshe-la.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.297
If Geshe-la's disconnected from Geshe-la,

00:06:30.297 --> 00:06:33.383
and Geshe-la can go moment
to moment like that,

00:06:33.383 --> 00:06:35.390
then Geshe-la's body and mind

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:37.290
can become Tim's body and mind,

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:41.107
and I can go over there
and join Tim's sansara.

00:06:41.107 --> 00:06:43.080
Right, got it?

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:46.060
If they're separated, anything can happen

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:48.290
and it can't be connected.

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:50.260
It cannot be a flow.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.093
- Why?

00:06:51.093 --> 00:06:52.720
- Because that would be unchanging,

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.370
and then you don't have
different lifetimes.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.770
It's just, you're stuck in
the same moment all the time,

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:59.985
like gopher's day, what's it called?

00:06:59.985 --> 00:07:03.636
- [Woman] Groundhog Day.
- Groundhog Day, right. [laughs]

00:07:03.636 --> 00:07:06.403
All right, next verse.

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:10.620
Where is that?

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.837
Oh, we are supposed to
have a picture, right?

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:16.970
Let's do the circle, or the second,

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:20.810
I see it's the second clock.

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:25.810
And Choney Lama says, look,
if Geshe-la's body and mind

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.870
only lasts for one millisecond,

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:31.950
how could it have time to go in a circle?

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.850
There's no circle if
there's only a single point.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.820
You can't draw a circle with single point,

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:38.980
with one single point.

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:41.403
All right, next verse.

00:07:44.693 --> 00:07:48.151
,SEMS CAN LA YANG RIM 'DI MTSUNGS,

00:07:48.151 --> 00:07:50.818
,SEMS CAN LA YANG RIM 'DI MTSUNGS,

00:07:51.923 --> 00:07:55.140
SEMS CAN means a living being.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:56.560
You can say sentient being,

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:59.800
I don't like the word
because it's not English.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:02.030
We don't say that in English.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:06.090
How's your sentient being mother?

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:09.514
So anyway, it's just a living being.

00:08:09.514 --> 00:08:13.949
SEMS CAN LA YANG, RIM
means what? Like Lam Rim.

00:08:13.949 --> 00:08:15.090
Steps, okay.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:20.090
And in Nagarjuna, RIM
has a special meaning,

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:24.763
and it means the steps to
an argument I just gave you.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:29.060
You know, those steps to
the last argument is called,

00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:30.820
in Nagarjuna, is called RIM.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:33.060
When you see RIM in Nagarjuna,

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:36.000
think: steps to my last argument.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.310
So what's it mean here?

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:43.080
If you say the person, if
you say what travels around

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.570
the circle, the Wheel of Life,

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:47.710
is not Geshe-la's body and mind,

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:52.710
but it's rather Geshe-la,

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:54.960
then RIM MTSUNGS, same argument.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.510
Go back to the same
argument. Which is what?

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:00.160
What's the first question Nagarjuna asked?

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:03.860
Now, don't forget, we
finished body and mind,

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:07.250
now the guy says, "Okay, okay,
body and mind cannot circle.

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:10.650
So Geshe-la circles, it's Geshe-la."

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:13.550
Okay, so let's do the same arguments.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.470
We asked him two questions.

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:19.330
If you say it's Geshe-la that's
circling around in sansara,

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:23.840
are you talking about a
Geshe-la who is unchanging?

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:26.440
He starts with unchanging,
I don't know why.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:28.690
- Are you talking about a
Geshe-la who is unchanging?

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:31.190
- Oh yeah, yeah, it's Geshe-la unchanging.

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:32.830
- Then how can he go in a circle,

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:33.663
because he's in the
same point all the time

00:09:33.663 --> 00:09:35.690
because he's the same guy.

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:38.940
He doesn't become an animal
or a deva or hell being,

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:40.570
he's just always Geshe-la.

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:43.360
So he can't, he can't change.

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.387
So what's his second RIM PA?

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.110
Or are you saying Geshe-la is

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.100
changing?

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:53.920
In which case he is random
moments of Geshe-la.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:55.640
And then in that case,

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:58.380
which we already proved
with our touching arguments,

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:02.690
contact arguments, then
there's no necessary connection

00:10:02.690 --> 00:10:05.100
between Geshe-la moment one
and Geshe-la moment two.

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:08.330
Geshe-la moment one could
become Tim moment two.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:10.260
And then who's circling?

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:14.011
Therefore, nobody's in sansara.

00:10:14.011 --> 00:10:16.740
Nobody's traveling
around the Wheel of Life.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:17.573
- Why?

00:10:17.573 --> 00:10:19.400
- It's not Geshe-la's body and mind,

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.010
and it's not Geshe-la. - Why?

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.390
- Because it's not
Geshe-la's body and mind

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:23.570
which is changing or unchanging,

00:10:23.570 --> 00:10:24.953
and it's not Geshe-la who's
changing or unchanging.

00:10:24.953 --> 00:10:29.810
There's nothing else.
Nobody's circling in sansara.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:32.380
All right, we got a picture.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:36.697
By the way, Choney Lama
likes to go to the idea of...

00:10:36.697 --> 00:10:40.340
He says, "Don't forget
when we say Geshe-la,

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:42.980
as opposed to Geshe-la's body and mind,

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:47.270
we're kind of talking about a soul.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:50.810
Is there some mega Geshe-la

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:53.690
who continues from birth to birth.

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:55.430
He wouldn't look like Geshe-la.

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:58.417
It's independent of body and mind.

00:10:58.417 --> 00:11:03.417
There's some inner soul
or essence of Geshe-la

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:07.040
which takes different
bodies and minds, right?

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.750
Which throws, who dumps
the old body and mind

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.000
and takes a new body and mind.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:12.100
So there's some kind of Geshe-la

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.570
independent of Geshe-la's body and mind.

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:19.210
There's a third part to
Geshe-la which is, you know,

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:22.500
"super inner Geshe-la",
and then the inner Geshe-la

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:26.320
takes bodies and minds,
and keeps going like that.

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:29.338
That's what the second argument's about.

00:11:29.338 --> 00:11:31.580
[students speaking indistinctly]

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:32.555
We're going to get there.

00:11:32.555 --> 00:11:34.180
In fact, that's the whole chapter.

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:36.920
Don't cheat, all right, here we go.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.730
That's the whole chapter actually.

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:39.670
Good question.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.986
All right, here we go.

00:11:43.661 --> 00:11:45.452
Next verse.

00:11:49.117 --> 00:11:50.858
,GAL TE GANG ZAG 'KHOR ZHE NA,

00:11:50.858 --> 00:11:53.299
,PHUNG PO SKYE MCHED KHAMS RNAMS LA,

00:11:53.299 --> 00:11:56.140
,DE NI RNAM PA LNGAS BTZAL NA,

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:59.600
,MED NA GANG ZHIG 'KHOR BAR 'GYUR,

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:02.770
This part has two verses.
Here's the first verse.

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:04.640
GAL TE GANG ZAG 'KHOR ZHE NA

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:05.960
Then the guy's insistent.

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:08.230
No, it's Geshe-la.

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:11.496
The GANG ZAG, the PURUṢA (PURUSHA).

00:12:11.496 --> 00:12:14.680
It's Geshe-la that goes from life to life.

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:19.680
He dumps bodies and minds and
he takes new bodies and minds.

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:21.990
It's like some guy in high
school with his girlfriends

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:24.850
or some lady in high
school with her boyfriends.

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:27.200
He dumps one body and mind
and then he takes another one,

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:28.610
then he takes another one.

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:31.550
But he continues through
high school, right?

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:36.550
Okay, so the guy says
no, no, it is Geshe-la

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:40.640
who goes from lifetime to lifetime.

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:44.300
Then let's examine Geshe-la's relationship

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:45.850
with his body and mind.

00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:50.850
Let's examine Geshe-la's, if
it's Geshe-la who keeps going

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:54.660
and getting rid of this body and mind

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.390
and picking up a new body and mind,

00:12:56.390 --> 00:12:57.810
well then what's the relationship

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:00.790
between Geshe-la and the body and mind?

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:02.470
Because there are some relationships

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:04.550
he cannot have with the body and mind

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:07.980
and still switch bodies and minds.

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:10.560
If Geshe-la is the body and mind,

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:12.590
then he can't dump the body and mind

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:15.263
and go to the next birth
because he would be gone.

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:20.330
If he is his body and
mind, and he gives up

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:23.090
a body and mind to take
on the next body and mind,

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:25.510
then Geshe-la cannot be the body and mind.

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:28.170
He's got to be some super
guy who takes bodies

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.580
and takes minds, right?

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:33.590
So what's the relationship?
Nagarjuna says, "Okay, okay".

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:34.670
Geshe-la keeps going, right?

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:35.837
- Yeah.

00:13:35.837 --> 00:13:37.380
- Geshe-la takes bodies and minds?

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:38.213
- Right.

00:13:38.213 --> 00:13:40.780
- So Geshe-la cannot be
his body and mind, right?

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:41.613
- Why?

00:13:41.613 --> 00:13:44.010
- Because he dumps them and
then he goes somewhere else.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:46.643
If he was his body and mind and
he dumped his body and mind,

00:13:46.643 --> 00:13:49.016
he'd be gone.

00:13:49.016 --> 00:13:49.849
Got it?

00:13:49.849 --> 00:13:51.787
There's no Geshe-la who
takes a body and mind

00:13:51.787 --> 00:13:53.740
because he is his body and mind.

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:56.280
We better look at the relationship

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:59.240
between Geshe-la and his body and mind.

00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:01.800
And then he says RNAM PA LNGAS BCOL

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:05.170
all the texts say RNAM PA LNGAS BCOL

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:08.363
which is total misspelling.

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:11.707
By the way, I got to fix it.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:14.639
So Tim, if you can imagine the letter

00:14:14.639 --> 00:14:17.836
CA - ཅ, first column,

00:14:17.836 --> 00:14:22.419
with a naro is CO - ཅོ, right?

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:26.010
But if you draw the
naro with only one horn.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:28.260
By the way, naro means horns.

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:29.720
So then what's it become?

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:33.180
A CA with a little flag on the side,

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.510
becomes TZA - ཙ, yeah, okay.

00:14:35.510 --> 00:14:37.960
All the texts say BCOL - བཅོལ,

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:41.020
and they're all wrong, it's a BTZAL- བཙལ.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:42.810
Okay, so that's the first problem.

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:44.586
You can spend two days looking up

00:14:44.586 --> 00:14:45.660
BCOLs in dictionaries,

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:47.210
and you won't figure it out.

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:50.090
And all the carvings are wrong.

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:53.578
Which is irritating for somebody.

00:14:53.578 --> 00:14:57.220
DE NI RNAM PA LNGAS
BTZAL NA, okay? If you...

00:14:58.469 --> 00:15:00.905
BTZAL means like PHYAG 'TSAL.

00:15:00.905 --> 00:15:02.478
What's 'TSAL in PHYAG 'TSAL?

00:15:02.478 --> 00:15:03.503
[students responding indistinctly]

00:15:03.503 --> 00:15:06.400
But what's it really mean?

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:09.491
To seek a boon from the hand of Lama.

00:15:09.491 --> 00:15:11.710
So BTZAL means to seek, to look.

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:13.897
So here it means to look.

00:15:13.897 --> 00:15:16.150
RNAM PA LNGA -- five different ways.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:20.060
There's five different
possible relationships

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:23.010
between Michael and
Michael's body and mind.

00:15:23.010 --> 00:15:24.610
Let's look at all five.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:28.100
If you say it's Michael who
goes from birth to birth

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:30.690
and he picks up new bodies and minds,

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:33.970
then let's look at the
possible relationships

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:35.840
between Michael and his body and mind.

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:38.730
Now Nagarjuna doesn't...

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:39.980
[students responding indistinctly]

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:42.810
tell you what the five are. [laughs]

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:45.680
He never mentions the five.

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:47.160
He never tells you what's the five.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.000
So here's Geshe-la, you
know, late at night,

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:52.790
oh my God, where's the five?

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:55.237
What do you do when you're
Geshe-la and it's late at night

00:15:55.237 --> 00:15:57.568
and you have to talk in the morning?

00:15:57.568 --> 00:15:58.500
[students responding indistinctly]

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.750
You go to Gofer. You go to the database.

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.740
And I went to the database

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:08.740
and the first answer I got was Rendawa.

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:11.650
We call Jetsun Rendawa.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.670
Who's Jetsun Rendawa, do you know?

00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:17.730
He's a Sakya master who was
the teacher of Tsongkapa.

00:16:17.730 --> 00:16:20.410
He's one of the main
teachers of Tsongkapa.

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:23.240
And they started out as
teacher and disciple,

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:26.210
later they teamed up as a teaching team

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:28.090
and they used to teach Vinaya together

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.230
and stuff like that.

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:31.700
So, and by the way, Rendawa wrote

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:35.653
an extraordinary commentary
to the Letter to a Friend.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:41.473
Short, sweet, precise.

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:45.840
So anyway, the first... and
he also wrote a commentary

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:49.940
to Nagarjuna's Wisdom,
which is short and precise,

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:51.940
concise and precise.

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:55.150
So, you know, first I went there,

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:57.640
and I worked on him for a while,

00:16:57.640 --> 00:17:00.877
and then I went to Tsongkapa
who wrote a commentary

00:17:00.877 --> 00:17:04.313
on Nagarjuna's "Wisdom", called...

00:17:05.945 --> 00:17:06.778
- [Woman] Ocean.

00:17:06.778 --> 00:17:08.428
- Yeah, the Ocean of Reasoning.

00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:12.230
You know, that's the ship that we're in.

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:14.920
We're trying to cross that ocean.

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:19.420
And so altogether I got some good answers.

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:23.040
And that's the beautiful
thing about this text,

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.800
everyone has tried to explain it,

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:29.710
and it's hard, it's really hard.

00:17:29.710 --> 00:17:33.420
So there's maybe hundreds of
commentaries on this text.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:38.910
Chandrakirti tried to explain it, right?

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:41.080
So here we go.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:44.830
So here's the five possible relationships

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:48.490
between Michael and
Michael's body and mind.

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:52.570
Here's the five. And where did I end up?

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:57.570
Oh, to be fair to Nagarjuna,
he already gave us the five

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:01.799
in his text, and we forgot.

00:18:01.799 --> 00:18:03.420
He gave it long ago.

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:05.530
He was talking about the relationship

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:07.418
between something and something.

00:18:07.418 --> 00:18:08.990
What is it?

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:11.210
Between the fire and the firewood,

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:13.990
and he already covered this point.

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:17.250
That's where, that's
why, he's not being lazy

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:21.260
when he says there's five
possible relationships.

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:23.060
He already covered this point

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:25.160
between the fire and the firewood.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:26.870
He already covered this point.

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:30.150
So he's probably sitting impatiently

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:32.610
saying, "Don't ask me stupid,

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:37.250
go back to verse #14 in
chapter 10." I went and got it,

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:38.940
and "I discussed it already there.

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:41.260
So don't tell me I didn't
tell you what the five are.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:44.720
I was hoping you would remember."

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:47.583
So here they are, and you know,

00:18:47.583 --> 00:18:51.390
you can go through them quickly
and you say, yeah, yeah,

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:53.150
and then you just don't
think about it anymore.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:55.499
But let's think about it carefully.

00:18:57.649 --> 00:19:02.007
Let's start with Tim. Is
Tim his body and mind?

00:19:04.308 --> 00:19:06.400
In this discussion.

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:10.200
Don't forget, the discussion
is in the context of

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:12.020
how does Tim go from birth to birth

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:13.990
in the Wheel of Life.

00:19:13.990 --> 00:19:17.365
So this is a pretty easy question.

00:19:17.365 --> 00:19:18.198
Is Tim,

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:22.390
Is Tim's body and Tim's mind right now,

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:24.728
is that all there is to Tim?

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:29.120
No, because if it dies, then Tim's gone

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:30.760
and there's no one to go through sansara.

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:35.760
So it can't be that Tim
equals Tim's body and mind

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:38.760
because somebody has to
take the body and mind

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:41.270
and somebody has to
drop the body and mind.

00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:43.575
Let's go on to Pachi, number two.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:49.470
Pachi. Is Pachi completely
separate from his body and mind?

00:19:55.030 --> 00:19:58.305
Look, he just fell off his
body and mind [laughs].

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:01.520
No, he has to have some connection, right?

00:20:01.520 --> 00:20:03.160
There has to be some connection, right?

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:05.960
Otherwise you would be Tim.

00:20:05.960 --> 00:20:08.500
Otherwise Pachi would
be Tim. I mean he'd just

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:11.620
glom on to the nearest
body and mind [laughs].

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:16.543
So there's got to be some Pachi

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:19.934
who's not separate from his body and mind.

00:20:19.934 --> 00:20:21.284
There has to be a Pachi who

00:20:21.284 --> 00:20:23.700
has some kind of connection
with his body and mind.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.400
You can say there's a separate Pachi

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:28.270
from his body and mind,
but somehow he has to be

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:31.172
intertwined with his body and mind.

00:20:31.172 --> 00:20:33.046
Otherwise he'd just get intertwined

00:20:33.046 --> 00:20:34.184
with Rebecca's body and mind,

00:20:34.184 --> 00:20:35.383
and then you'd have trouble combing

00:20:35.383 --> 00:20:37.630
your hair and everything.

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:40.083
And you would have a beard and...

00:20:40.083 --> 00:20:43.335
There's all kinds of
philosophical problems. [laughs]

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:49.280
Okay, so Tim is not his body and mind,

00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:52.390
but Pachi is not completely
separate from his body and mind.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:53.820
He's got some connection to it.

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:55.826
Okay, third possibility.

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:03.230
Does Rebecca's body and
mind somehow have Rebecca?

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:09.450
You see, let's switch it this way.

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:13.190
So we're not talking about does
Rebecca have body and mind.

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:15.215
Does the body and mind over there

00:21:15.215 --> 00:21:18.465
somehow reach out and hold Rebecca?

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:22.081
That's a weird idea.

00:21:22.081 --> 00:21:24.740
That's the third possibility of the five.

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:28.740
Somehow your body and
mind have attracted you,

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:33.560
and your body and mind's
gravity sucked in Rebecca,

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:36.250
and Rebecca's stuck to
Rebecca's body and mind.

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:39.040
That's the third possibility,
which is kind of silly,

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:41.093
but it's not completely silly.

00:21:44.036 --> 00:21:46.203
A fourth possibility, Pau ready?

00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:51.630
Pau doesn't depend on her body and mind.

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.100
You can do anything to her body and mind,

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:56.803
and it doesn't effect Pau.

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:00.680
You can get a virus, you
can get a vaccination,

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:02.533
and Pau doesn't care.

00:22:03.446 --> 00:22:06.460
Pau's a different entity
from body and mind.

00:22:06.460 --> 00:22:10.090
But Pau doesn't rest on her body and mind.

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:11.977
That's the fourth possibility, right?

00:22:11.977 --> 00:22:12.977
We've got four, right?

00:22:12.977 --> 00:22:16.293
One, two, three, four.
Okay, Christina, you ready?

00:22:18.680 --> 00:22:22.203
Christina's body and mind
don't depend on Christina.

00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:25.860
So Christina can go away and
Christina's body and mind

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:28.523
will still be in the chair, typing away.

00:22:30.350 --> 00:22:33.080
Okay, all right, that's
the fifth possibility.

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:38.080
And all five possibilities
are kind of on untenable.

00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:40.800
They're not, they're kind of impossible.

00:22:40.800 --> 00:22:43.130
It doesn't seem possible.

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:46.350
What were you thinking when you thought

00:22:46.350 --> 00:22:48.492
you were traveling through sansara?

00:22:48.492 --> 00:22:51.100
What were you thinking
was your relationship

00:22:51.100 --> 00:22:52.240
to your body and mind?

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:53.885
Could you dump your body and mind

00:22:53.885 --> 00:22:56.460
and there's still something
about you that can go on

00:22:56.460 --> 00:22:57.720
and take another body and mind?

00:22:57.720 --> 00:23:00.610
Can you exist without a body and mind?

00:23:00.610 --> 00:23:03.730
Can the body and mind exist without you?

00:23:03.730 --> 00:23:05.430
Can it go on without you?

00:23:05.430 --> 00:23:09.450
You know, when you think about

00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:10.720
going through the Wheel of Life,

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:15.185
traveling through sansara, you
didn't really think it out.

00:23:15.185 --> 00:23:17.000
That's what Nagarjuna's saying.

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:19.100
Maybe you have some idea.

00:23:19.100 --> 00:23:20.410
I think most of us feel,

00:23:20.410 --> 00:23:22.180
at least I grew up in a Christian culture,

00:23:22.180 --> 00:23:24.330
Judeo-Christian culture.

00:23:24.330 --> 00:23:27.280
I feel like there's some Michael's soul

00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:29.940
that takes the body and mind
and holds it for a while

00:23:29.940 --> 00:23:33.190
and then they get separated
and the soul goes on

00:23:33.190 --> 00:23:35.404
and then the soul has to
find a new body and mind,

00:23:35.404 --> 00:23:38.136
or something like that.

00:23:39.090 --> 00:23:41.740
And in that case, you could do
things to the body and mind,

00:23:41.740 --> 00:23:43.580
you could abuse the body and mind,

00:23:43.580 --> 00:23:46.120
and the soul is somehow beyond all that.

00:23:46.120 --> 00:23:49.620
Nothing happens to the
soul, something like that.

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:53.010
The Judeo-Christian culture

00:23:53.010 --> 00:23:56.220
has an opinion on this question.

00:23:56.220 --> 00:23:59.230
And so we have it because
we grew up in this culture.

00:23:59.230 --> 00:24:02.348
But if you really examine
it, is it defensible?

00:24:02.348 --> 00:24:04.173
Is it make sense?

00:24:05.330 --> 00:24:10.030
Are you totally independent
from your body and mind?

00:24:10.030 --> 00:24:12.928
Is there a Rebecca which is totally,

00:24:14.010 --> 00:24:16.820
is totally unaffected
by the body and mind?

00:24:19.337 --> 00:24:22.210
All right, and if you're interested,

00:24:22.210 --> 00:24:25.060
go back to verse 14 of chapter 10

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:29.560
where they discuss whether
the wood is the fire,

00:24:29.560 --> 00:24:31.440
and that's the same argument.

00:24:31.440 --> 00:24:33.390
And that's why Nagarjuna didn't bother.

00:24:38.967 --> 00:24:43.560
GAL TE MANG POS BKUR BA ,I'm sorry, no.

00:24:43.560 --> 00:24:45.110
We finished that.

00:24:46.801 --> 00:24:47.634
All right.

00:24:49.410 --> 00:24:50.870
Let's go to...

00:24:52.652 --> 00:24:53.860
[student speaking indistinctly]

00:24:53.860 --> 00:24:54.693
'DU BYED

00:24:57.260 --> 00:25:01.394
We didn't do NYE BAR LEN, verse three?

00:25:02.230 --> 00:25:04.910
Oh right, you're right, the second half.

00:25:04.910 --> 00:25:06.531
Oh yeah, that's a nasty one.

00:25:06.531 --> 00:25:07.800
[laughing]

00:25:07.800 --> 00:25:10.950
I don't know why I skipped it.

00:25:11.850 --> 00:25:14.963
Let's go back, I know
what you're talking about.

00:25:17.600 --> 00:25:20.442
,NYE BAR LEN NAS NYER LEN PAR,

00:25:20.442 --> 00:25:22.550
,'KHOR NA SRID PA MED PAR 'GYUR,

00:25:22.550 --> 00:25:24.332
,SRID MED NYE BAR LEN MED NA,

00:25:24.332 --> 00:25:27.680
,DE GANG CI ZHIG 'KHOR BAR 'GYUR,

00:25:27.680 --> 00:25:30.030
This is tricky because NYE BAR LEN PA

00:25:30.030 --> 00:25:33.870
is a very difficult word
in Buddhist philosophy

00:25:33.870 --> 00:25:38.082
which means to take on closely.

00:25:38.082 --> 00:25:39.380
NYE BAR LEN PA

00:25:39.380 --> 00:25:44.207
But it means to take on a
new body and mind at rebirth.

00:25:44.207 --> 00:25:48.688
So, okay, so even that word suggests what?

00:25:49.901 --> 00:25:51.170
[students responding indistinctly]

00:25:51.170 --> 00:25:53.070
Yeah, somebody takes it on.

00:25:53.070 --> 00:25:56.730
Okay, so the Buddhist, the
ancient Buddhist expression

00:25:56.730 --> 00:26:01.657
for rebirth is called
embracing another one.

00:26:04.140 --> 00:26:06.310
It's called embracing another one.

00:26:06.310 --> 00:26:10.650
So it means another body and mind.

00:26:10.650 --> 00:26:15.420
So then Nagarjuna uses
it for the word rebirth.

00:26:15.420 --> 00:26:17.270
He uses it for the word rebirth.

00:26:17.270 --> 00:26:21.900
He says, "So is it that a rebirth...

00:26:21.900 --> 00:26:23.720
What happens from rebirth to rebirth?

00:26:23.720 --> 00:26:26.160
Let's look at that, and then we can decide

00:26:26.160 --> 00:26:30.060
your relationship. We can
decide the relationship

00:26:30.060 --> 00:26:33.850
of your body and mind with you.

00:26:33.850 --> 00:26:36.820
Let's look at how you go
from rebirth to rebirth,

00:26:36.820 --> 00:26:38.770
and then we can decide
what's the relationship

00:26:38.770 --> 00:26:42.083
between Tim and Tim's body and mind.

00:26:43.030 --> 00:26:46.190
So he says here NYE BAR
LEN NAS NYER LEN PAR

00:26:46.190 --> 00:26:49.220
when you go from one identity
to another, for example,

00:26:49.220 --> 00:26:52.850
and then Choney Lama says,
I don't know why he says,

00:26:52.850 --> 00:26:57.010
"If you go from a human birth
to a deva", to a deva birth,

00:26:57.010 --> 00:27:01.373
to a divine, temporary
suffering being birth,

00:27:02.780 --> 00:27:05.390
which kind of assumes that
we are meditating. Okay?

00:27:05.390 --> 00:27:09.530
'KHOR NA SRID PA MED PAR 'GYUR,

00:27:09.530 --> 00:27:12.351
then there's no SRID PA in 'KHOR BA.

00:27:12.351 --> 00:27:15.604
'KHOR BA means sansara,

00:27:15.604 --> 00:27:19.440
SRID PA here means, and
again you need Choney Lama.

00:27:19.440 --> 00:27:21.310
It doesn't mean SRID PA

00:27:21.310 --> 00:27:25.435
which means sansara,
like SRID PA'I 'KHOR LO,

00:27:25.435 --> 00:27:30.010
BHAVACAKRA, the Wheel of Life,
it doesn't mean that here.

00:27:30.010 --> 00:27:32.070
Here it means BAR SRID.

00:27:32.070 --> 00:27:33.987
And since you guys studied Abhidharma

00:27:33.987 --> 00:27:38.987
you know what's a BAR
SRID, BAR DO SRID PA.

00:27:39.340 --> 00:27:40.490
[students responding indistinctly]

00:27:40.490 --> 00:27:44.300
A being in the BAR DO, yeah,
it's called a BAR SRID.

00:27:44.300 --> 00:27:47.166
It's called a BAR guy.

00:27:47.166 --> 00:27:48.390
[laughs] BAR guy.

00:27:48.390 --> 00:27:51.496
It's not that kind of bar guy.

00:27:51.496 --> 00:27:53.045
BAR SRID

00:27:53.045 --> 00:27:56.210
So KHOR NA SRID PA MED PAR 'GYUR

00:27:56.210 --> 00:28:00.457
If you drop, if you drop, how do you say?

00:28:02.190 --> 00:28:04.960
if you drop one body and mind

00:28:04.960 --> 00:28:08.400
and then take on another body
and mind in the next moment,

00:28:08.400 --> 00:28:10.042
then there's no BAR DO.

00:28:10.880 --> 00:28:12.115
That's what he's saying.

00:28:12.115 --> 00:28:14.630
Nagarjuna's saying, "Look,
what happens when you,

00:28:14.630 --> 00:28:17.080
how do you go from one
birth to another birth?"

00:28:17.080 --> 00:28:18.270
Oh, and the other guy says,

00:28:18.270 --> 00:28:19.637
"Well, you just drop your body and mind

00:28:19.637 --> 00:28:23.080
and then you pick up a new
one in the next millisecond."

00:28:23.080 --> 00:28:25.008
- Okay, then there's no BAR DO

00:28:25.008 --> 00:28:27.530
which is against Buddhist teaching.

00:28:27.530 --> 00:28:29.070
There should be a BAR DO.

00:28:29.070 --> 00:28:34.070
There should be a... for
most kinds of rebirth.

00:28:34.130 --> 00:28:37.007
Then the guy says, no, no, no.

00:28:37.007 --> 00:28:39.540
,SRID MED NYE BAR LEN MED NA,

00:28:42.806 --> 00:28:44.122
,SRID MED NYE BAR LEN MED NA,

00:28:44.122 --> 00:28:47.800
,DE GANG CI ZHIG 'KHOR BAR 'GYUR,

00:28:47.800 --> 00:28:52.670
How can you say there's a cycle of rebirth

00:28:52.670 --> 00:28:55.751
if there's an interruption
between the rebirth?

00:28:56.720 --> 00:29:01.720
How can you say there's a
constant continuation of rebirth

00:29:02.160 --> 00:29:05.630
if it's a discontinuation?

00:29:05.630 --> 00:29:07.840
If you say no, no, no, there's a BAR DO,

00:29:07.840 --> 00:29:10.090
well then there's no connection,

00:29:10.090 --> 00:29:12.480
no necessary connection between

00:29:12.480 --> 00:29:15.100
dropping this body and
mind, and picking up

00:29:15.100 --> 00:29:17.690
your next body and mind,
because there's a gap.

00:29:17.690 --> 00:29:20.650
And you can't have a
circle where there're gaps.

00:29:20.650 --> 00:29:22.120
That doesn't make a circle.

00:29:22.120 --> 00:29:24.817
Circles should be [vocalizing],

00:29:25.820 --> 00:29:26.761
They should go like that.

00:29:26.761 --> 00:29:31.570
If there is a BAR DO,
then there's no 'KHOR BA.

00:29:31.570 --> 00:29:33.930
If you drop your body and mind,

00:29:33.930 --> 00:29:37.270
and there's a gap until you
pick up your new body and mind,

00:29:37.270 --> 00:29:39.210
then you can't have a cycle.

00:29:39.210 --> 00:29:44.158
That's just a bunch of interrupted
vignettes or something.

00:29:44.158 --> 00:29:46.360
It's not a cycle.

00:29:46.360 --> 00:29:48.780
It doesn't fit the meaning of a cycle.

00:29:48.780 --> 00:29:50.521
Cycles should be [vocalizing], same thing

00:29:50.521 --> 00:29:51.779
over and over again, like, I don't know,

00:29:51.779 --> 00:29:55.170
troubles with the tech
equipment or something.

00:29:55.170 --> 00:29:58.800
you know, shit just keeps happening.

00:29:58.800 --> 00:30:00.990
Sorry, I'm not saying it did, I'm saying,

00:30:00.990 --> 00:30:02.600
by the way I'm very grateful for the tech,

00:30:02.600 --> 00:30:05.571
God bless the tech.

00:30:07.560 --> 00:30:11.943
So we covered that second verse.
Let's go to the next verse.

00:30:17.480 --> 00:30:19.933
Yeah, and it's a very interesting segue.

00:30:21.650 --> 00:30:26.020
Sometimes Nagarjuna just
moves on to another topic,

00:30:26.020 --> 00:30:28.950
meaning he thinks the case is closed.

00:30:28.950 --> 00:30:32.340
We're like... and he's
like, "Come on, you got it,

00:30:32.340 --> 00:30:33.575
you guys got it.

00:30:33.575 --> 00:30:37.490
Nobody takes on the body and
mind and the body and mind

00:30:37.490 --> 00:30:39.430
doesn't have anybody to take it on.

00:30:39.430 --> 00:30:40.910
Let's move on."
[students laughing]

00:30:40.910 --> 00:30:43.167
Okay, and you're like oh, wait!

00:30:44.590 --> 00:30:46.315
So here we go to the next verse.

00:30:46.315 --> 00:30:49.446
He's moving to a huge separate topic.

00:30:49.446 --> 00:30:51.729
,'DU BYED MYA NGAN 'DA' BAR NI,

00:30:51.729 --> 00:30:54.296
,JI LTA BUR YANG MI 'THAD DO,

00:30:54.296 --> 00:30:56.378
,SEMS CAN MYA NGAN 'DA' BAR YANG,

00:30:56.378 --> 00:30:58.745
,JI LTA BUR YANG 'THAD MI 'GYUR,

00:30:58.745 --> 00:31:01.280
Let's stop talking about who it is

00:31:01.280 --> 00:31:03.810
that takes on bodies and minds.

00:31:03.810 --> 00:31:08.070
Let's start talking about who
it is that reaches nirvana.

00:31:08.070 --> 00:31:10.070
Who breaks out of this cycle?

00:31:10.070 --> 00:31:12.920
What's happening then?

00:31:12.920 --> 00:31:15.220
What's happening when you
break out of the cycle?

00:31:15.220 --> 00:31:18.680
We discussed the cycle,
it doesn't make sense.

00:31:18.680 --> 00:31:21.450
You cannot take on a body and mind

00:31:21.450 --> 00:31:23.620
and you cannot not take
on a body and mind.

00:31:23.620 --> 00:31:25.898
Something's fishy.

00:31:26.760 --> 00:31:29.860
Enough, let's go on to,
well who gets enlightened,

00:31:29.860 --> 00:31:31.751
who gets to nirvana?

00:31:31.751 --> 00:31:33.870
'DU BYED MYA NGAN 'DA' BAR NI

00:31:33.870 --> 00:31:36.190
What's 'DU BYED mean this chapter?

00:31:36.190 --> 00:31:37.343
For $100.

00:31:39.460 --> 00:31:40.493
Factor.

00:31:41.520 --> 00:31:44.437
But what's it mean in this chapter?

00:31:46.350 --> 00:31:48.108
Cancel the bet.

00:31:48.108 --> 00:31:50.410
PHUNG PO -- the body and mind.

00:31:50.410 --> 00:31:53.730
So the word factors in this chapter

00:31:53.730 --> 00:31:55.270
refers to your body and mind.

00:31:55.270 --> 00:31:59.160
It just means changing stuff,
the changing part of Rebecca.

00:31:59.160 --> 00:32:02.803
Rebecca as a soul is this stainless steel,

00:32:03.690 --> 00:32:08.690
unchanging egg shape, and
then Rebecca's body and mind,

00:32:10.340 --> 00:32:13.020
and he calls it changing
stuff about Rebecca,

00:32:13.020 --> 00:32:15.036
which is the stuff you
take on and you drop

00:32:15.036 --> 00:32:15.920
from life to life.

00:32:15.920 --> 00:32:19.150
So he says, look, does the,

00:32:19.150 --> 00:32:24.150
is it Rebecca's body and
mind that goes to nirvana?

00:32:24.440 --> 00:32:27.900
What part of Rebecca goes to nirvana?

00:32:27.900 --> 00:32:30.302
Is it Rebecca's body and mind?

00:32:30.302 --> 00:32:34.490
JI LTA BUR YANG MI 'THAD DO

00:32:36.891 --> 00:32:38.723
Now, now it's this kind
of frustrating thing

00:32:38.723 --> 00:32:40.140
with Nagarjuna.

00:32:40.140 --> 00:32:43.180
He says no, it's not Becky's body and mind

00:32:43.180 --> 00:32:44.290
that goes to nirvana.

00:32:44.290 --> 00:32:45.123
- Why?

00:32:45.123 --> 00:32:48.176
- Because it's self-existent, please.

00:32:50.303 --> 00:32:53.228
It's not her body and mind

00:32:53.228 --> 00:32:55.720
which blinks out or something.

00:32:55.720 --> 00:32:58.240
- Why?
- Because it's self-existent,

00:32:58.240 --> 00:33:00.850
it doesn't depend on anything else.

00:33:00.850 --> 00:33:02.930
It doesn't depend on mental seeds.

00:33:02.930 --> 00:33:06.713
It's coming from its own side.
It doesn't ever blink out.

00:33:08.210 --> 00:33:10.580
It's coming illogically from its own side,

00:33:10.580 --> 00:33:13.580
and it's going to stay
illogical from its own side.

00:33:13.580 --> 00:33:18.090
And nothing illogical's
going to make it disappear.

00:33:18.090 --> 00:33:22.982
It's an illogical, metal,
unchangeable egg shape

00:33:22.982 --> 00:33:24.790
called Rebecca.

00:33:24.790 --> 00:33:26.190
So forget it.

00:33:26.190 --> 00:33:28.670
And Nagarjuna's kind of
frustrating that way.

00:33:28.670 --> 00:33:30.870
This book is kind of frustrating that way.

00:33:30.870 --> 00:33:32.560
Whenever he gets in a corner, he says,

00:33:32.560 --> 00:33:35.290
"Well, anyway it can't happen."

00:33:35.290 --> 00:33:36.123
And you say, Why?

00:33:36.123 --> 00:33:38.100
And he says because you
think it's coming...

00:33:38.100 --> 00:33:39.800
because you think the
husband in the kitchen

00:33:39.800 --> 00:33:42.992
comes from his side. "na, na, na, na, na."

00:33:42.992 --> 00:33:44.430
[students laughing]

00:33:44.430 --> 00:33:46.233
Then you're like oh man, come on.

00:33:47.300 --> 00:33:50.600
If the husband in the kitchen

00:33:50.600 --> 00:33:54.040
is upset because he had traffic at work,

00:33:54.040 --> 00:33:54.873
then your...

00:33:57.840 --> 00:34:01.130
then your body and mind
cannot go to nirvana.

00:34:01.130 --> 00:34:02.150
That's his argument.

00:34:02.150 --> 00:34:05.460
If your husband is coming from his side,

00:34:05.460 --> 00:34:09.560
then your body and mind cannot
be what goes to nirvana.

00:34:09.560 --> 00:34:10.393
- Why?

00:34:10.393 --> 00:34:13.240
- Because it also exists
from it's own side,

00:34:13.240 --> 00:34:14.940
and it couldn't change.

00:34:14.940 --> 00:34:18.240
It couldn't reach some
elevated place called nirvana

00:34:18.240 --> 00:34:19.870
because it couldn't change,

00:34:19.870 --> 00:34:21.690
because it's coming from its own side.

00:34:21.690 --> 00:34:23.930
The only way anything can
change in the universe

00:34:23.930 --> 00:34:27.323
is if your mental seeds change. Got it?

00:34:28.340 --> 00:34:31.570
All right, then the guy changes the story.

00:34:31.570 --> 00:34:34.190
Oh, it's not Rebecca's body
and mind that goes to nirvana,

00:34:34.190 --> 00:34:37.746
it's... what's the other choice?

00:34:38.580 --> 00:34:40.623
It's not Rebecca's body and mind-

00:34:40.623 --> 00:34:41.456
- [Students] Rebecca.

00:34:41.456 --> 00:34:45.040
- It's Rebecca, which he
calls GANG ZAG, PARUSHA.

00:34:45.040 --> 00:34:47.010
- Oh no, no, no, I change, I change,

00:34:47.010 --> 00:34:50.900
it's not Rebecca's body and
mind that goes to nirvana,

00:34:50.900 --> 00:34:53.949
it's "Rebecca".

00:34:53.949 --> 00:34:55.282
MYA NGAN 'DA' YANG

00:34:55.282 --> 00:34:58.385
JI LTA BUR YANG 'THAD MI 'GYUR

00:34:58.385 --> 00:34:59.860
Same problem, please.

00:34:59.860 --> 00:35:02.210
Rebecca comes from her own side.

00:35:02.210 --> 00:35:05.255
She can't change. She can't go to nirvana.

00:35:06.180 --> 00:35:08.840
It's kind of using the
thing he's trying to prove

00:35:08.840 --> 00:35:11.180
in the argument, to prove
what he's trying to prove.

00:35:11.180 --> 00:35:13.810
It seems a little fishy,
but if it's fishy,

00:35:13.810 --> 00:35:16.769
he's proving what he said.

00:35:16.769 --> 00:35:18.420
[students responding indistinctly]

00:35:18.420 --> 00:35:20.781
Everything's fishy, okay.

00:35:21.710 --> 00:35:24.463
Yeah, and the picture is
just kind of artificial here,

00:35:25.530 --> 00:35:28.130
but it's to help you remember.

00:35:28.130 --> 00:35:33.053
Here's [laughs], here's
Rebecca's body and mind.

00:35:34.408 --> 00:35:36.677
It's supposed to be the mind and the body.

00:35:36.677 --> 00:35:38.347
And which one gets to nirvana?

00:35:38.347 --> 00:35:40.068
I don't know.

00:35:40.068 --> 00:35:41.401
All right.

00:35:43.310 --> 00:35:48.280
Choney Lama has a particularly
compelling, excuse me,

00:35:51.025 --> 00:35:54.200
has a particularly
compelling argument here,

00:35:54.200 --> 00:35:56.120
and I would like to read it.

00:35:56.120 --> 00:35:59.880
So sometimes it's nice to go
to Choney Lama, let him talk.

00:35:59.880 --> 00:36:02.917
We've just been letting Nagarjuna talk.

00:36:02.917 --> 00:36:06.333
'DIR 'KHOR MKHAN RANG
BZHIN GYIS MED PAR NGES NA

00:36:06.333 --> 00:36:09.720
If it is the case that the 'KHOR MKHAN,

00:36:10.697 --> 00:36:13.580
MKHAN, MKHAN is the...

00:36:15.350 --> 00:36:20.350
MKHAN is the word you add
to a verb to make it a doer,

00:36:20.700 --> 00:36:23.728
like a teacher would be a SLOB MKHAN.

00:36:23.728 --> 00:36:26.560
MKHAN is E-R in English, teach-er.

00:36:26.560 --> 00:36:30.000
You add E-R to teach, it
makes the person who teaches.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:31.930
In Tibetan you add MKHAN.

00:36:31.930 --> 00:36:34.408
So what's 'KHOR MKHAN?

00:36:34.408 --> 00:36:35.241
- [Woman] A circler.

00:36:35.241 --> 00:36:36.074
- The circler, yeah,

00:36:36.074 --> 00:36:38.810
the guy who goes around in sansara. Good.

00:36:38.810 --> 00:36:42.770
'KHOR MKHAN RANG BZHIN
GYIS MED PAR NGES NA

00:36:42.770 --> 00:36:45.733
Choney Lama's like, "Why
are we talking about,

00:36:46.960 --> 00:36:50.130
"why are we so obsessed
with this person who,

00:36:50.130 --> 00:36:52.970
"why are we obsessed with
figuring out who it is

00:36:52.970 --> 00:36:54.537
that goes through sansara?"

00:36:56.030 --> 00:36:58.013
Because if you can NGES PA,

00:36:58.013 --> 00:37:02.672
if you can ascertain that they are

00:37:02.672 --> 00:37:06.317
RANG BZHIN GYIS MED PA

00:37:06.317 --> 00:37:07.800
[students responding indistinctly]

00:37:07.800 --> 00:37:11.510
Yeah, if you can ascertain that the person

00:37:11.510 --> 00:37:14.970
who goes around sansara doesn't
exist from their own side,

00:37:14.970 --> 00:37:19.696
well then you can stop
going around sansara!

00:37:19.696 --> 00:37:21.800
You got it? It's very beautiful.

00:37:21.800 --> 00:37:23.580
I'll say it again.

00:37:23.580 --> 00:37:25.660
Choney Lama says, "Hey, you want to guess

00:37:25.660 --> 00:37:27.840
why we're obsessing about who it is

00:37:27.840 --> 00:37:29.620
that circles around in sansara?

00:37:29.620 --> 00:37:31.460
And we're like, "I don't know."

00:37:31.460 --> 00:37:32.830
He says, "Because we want to see

00:37:32.830 --> 00:37:34.700
that they don't have any
nature on their own."

00:37:34.700 --> 00:37:35.830
- Well, why?

00:37:35.830 --> 00:37:39.372
- Because then you don't have
to circle around sansara!

00:37:39.372 --> 00:37:41.430
It's a very beautiful argument.

00:37:41.430 --> 00:37:42.263
Got it?

00:37:44.130 --> 00:37:47.630
That's why we're having
this long discussion

00:37:47.630 --> 00:37:50.370
about who is it that
circles around sansara.

00:37:50.370 --> 00:37:52.910
Because by examining your relationship

00:37:52.910 --> 00:37:56.550
to your body and mind, you're
suddenly going to figure out

00:37:56.550 --> 00:38:00.080
that you are coming from
yourself, your seeds,

00:38:00.080 --> 00:38:03.720
and then you don't have to
circle around sansara. Yay!

00:38:03.720 --> 00:38:05.220
Okay.

00:38:05.220 --> 00:38:07.465
That's so Choney Lama.

00:38:07.465 --> 00:38:09.431
All right, next verse.

00:38:11.540 --> 00:38:15.382
Now he wants to talk about the concept of

00:38:15.382 --> 00:38:16.597
'CHING BA and GROL BA,

00:38:16.597 --> 00:38:18.590
and I'd like to skip
to the Sanskrit lesson

00:38:18.590 --> 00:38:21.330
which is the next slide.

00:38:21.330 --> 00:38:24.080
Mainly I do this for Christina

00:38:24.080 --> 00:38:26.160
because she appreciates it.

00:38:26.160 --> 00:38:28.620
So we're going to discuss
'CHING BA and GROL BA.

00:38:28.620 --> 00:38:33.620
This chapter is called
Bondage and Liberation.

00:38:33.800 --> 00:38:37.610
Shackles and Freedom,
or something like that.

00:38:37.610 --> 00:38:40.660
And we've been discussing
who is it that's shackled?

00:38:40.660 --> 00:38:43.090
Who is it that's in the handcuffs?

00:38:43.090 --> 00:38:45.240
And now let's go look
at the Sanskrit words

00:38:45.240 --> 00:38:48.390
that are being used here
because then you can

00:38:49.260 --> 00:38:51.610
learn some Sanskrit

00:38:51.610 --> 00:38:55.070
so when you become Medicine
Buddha, you can speak in Sanskrit.

00:38:55.070 --> 00:38:58.607
So here's the first word: BANDHA, BANDHA.

00:38:58.607 --> 00:39:00.450
We have them in yoga, right?

00:39:00.450 --> 00:39:02.953
Pau, what's a BANDHA?

00:39:02.953 --> 00:39:04.410
[students responding indistinctly]

00:39:04.410 --> 00:39:07.285
Yeah, a lock. We call it a lock.

00:39:07.285 --> 00:39:09.750
[students responding indistinctly]

00:39:09.750 --> 00:39:12.540
Yeah, similar. GRANTHI is more nasty,

00:39:12.540 --> 00:39:14.348
GRANTHI is like a knot in the channels.

00:39:14.348 --> 00:39:17.010
But BANDHA is a purposeful,

00:39:17.010 --> 00:39:20.013
somewhere down here, I don't
know, it's hard for me to do.

00:39:20.013 --> 00:39:24.550
You tighten up your belly,
that's a BANDHA, a lock.

00:39:24.550 --> 00:39:27.100
Okay, so BANDHA, technical
spelling is the same,

00:39:27.100 --> 00:39:31.770
it doesn't have any, it's
all English sound, BANDHA.

00:39:31.770 --> 00:39:34.056
The Tibetan is 'CHING BA.

00:39:35.850 --> 00:39:39.440
The way I learned 'CHING BA was
from the Tibetan newspapers,

00:39:39.440 --> 00:39:41.947
they kept talking about
@'CHING GROL DMAG MI

00:39:44.130 --> 00:39:46.620
People's Liberation Army.

00:39:46.620 --> 00:39:51.160
The word in Tibetan for
the Chinese National Army

00:39:51.160 --> 00:39:56.077
is @'CHING GROL DMAG MI,
shackle-freeing army.

00:39:58.117 --> 00:40:00.011
People's Liberation Army.

00:40:00.011 --> 00:40:02.250
So 'CHING means shackle.

00:40:02.250 --> 00:40:04.103
Okay, 'CHING BA.

00:40:06.720 --> 00:40:10.847
So the root is √BANDH,
and it means to bind.

00:40:10.847 --> 00:40:15.513
Hey Jigme, did you ever go
to the bus station in India,

00:40:15.513 --> 00:40:18.533
and everyone's on strike
and they're all saying,

00:40:18.533 --> 00:40:21.624
"BANDH KARO"

00:40:21.624 --> 00:40:23.869
We're on strike, we're on strike.

00:40:23.869 --> 00:40:28.053
BANDH means, shackle the buses
so they can't get anywhere.

00:40:29.271 --> 00:40:32.600
The Indo-European is
√BHENDH, and it came into

00:40:32.600 --> 00:40:35.163
bind, band, and bundle.

00:40:36.030 --> 00:40:38.870
Okay, so it's easy to see how BANDHA

00:40:38.870 --> 00:40:41.910
means being chained to sansara.

00:40:41.910 --> 00:40:43.442
Okay, now what's the opposite?

00:40:43.442 --> 00:40:46.063
Next slide is MUKTI or MOKṢA (MOKSHA).

00:40:47.760 --> 00:40:52.760
The SHA is a retroflex, right?

00:40:53.010 --> 00:40:55.610
You've got to turn your
tongue back, MOKSHA MOKSHA

00:40:56.818 --> 00:40:59.485
and the Tibetan is GROL
BA as in SGROL MA -- Tara.

00:41:01.440 --> 00:41:05.230
And the root is √muc or
√mokṣ which means to release.

00:41:05.230 --> 00:41:08.928
I think it's related
to the Indo-European...

00:41:11.547 --> 00:41:15.713
there's a MUC which means to be slimy,

00:41:16.550 --> 00:41:18.870
like mucus comes from that.

00:41:18.870 --> 00:41:21.730
And I think it means to
slide out of sansara,

00:41:21.730 --> 00:41:24.775
but I didn't put that here
because it's a little too much.

00:41:24.775 --> 00:41:26.730
[students laughing]

00:41:26.730 --> 00:41:31.130
On your [laughs]...

00:41:31.130 --> 00:41:32.880
And I think that all of them are related

00:41:32.880 --> 00:41:36.410
to the Indo-European
√mittere which means to,

00:41:36.410 --> 00:41:38.520
and you find it in Latin, right,

00:41:38.520 --> 00:41:43.520
to send a message, missive,
mission, to send somebody out.

00:41:43.520 --> 00:41:47.210
It means to liberate somebody, got it?

00:41:47.210 --> 00:41:49.540
All right, so let's go
back to the verse now

00:41:49.540 --> 00:41:52.446
which is going backwards in the slides.

00:41:52.446 --> 00:41:54.512
,SKYE 'JIG CHOS CAN 'DU BYED RNAMS,

00:41:54.512 --> 00:41:56.721
,MI 'CHING GROL BAR MI 'GYUR TE,

00:41:56.721 --> 00:41:58.850
Don't forget that 'DU BYED here

00:41:58.850 --> 00:42:01.430
means body and mind.

00:42:01.430 --> 00:42:05.220
Spelled a little differently.

00:42:05.220 --> 00:42:08.177
How could you remove shackles

00:42:10.642 --> 00:42:13.730
from a SKYE 'JIG?

00:42:13.730 --> 00:42:16.844
From a person who was going
in and out of existence.

00:42:16.844 --> 00:42:19.780
SKYE 'JIG -- minute by
minute, second by second.

00:42:19.780 --> 00:42:24.017
How could you liberate a person?

00:42:25.530 --> 00:42:29.490
How could you take chains off of a person

00:42:29.490 --> 00:42:31.690
which was either unchanging

00:42:31.690 --> 00:42:34.165
or changing millisecond by millisecond?

00:42:34.165 --> 00:42:37.020
You know, by the time you get
your hands on the shackles,

00:42:37.020 --> 00:42:39.280
they changed into somebody else.

00:42:39.280 --> 00:42:42.080
So how can you... Who is there?

00:42:42.080 --> 00:42:47.080
What body and mind is
there in a sustained way

00:42:47.610 --> 00:42:50.050
to take off their shackles?

00:42:50.050 --> 00:42:52.220
Because if they're in a sustained way,

00:42:52.220 --> 00:42:55.660
that means they're unchanging,
which is impossible.

00:42:55.660 --> 00:42:59.220
You can't take shackles off of a person

00:42:59.220 --> 00:43:03.000
who is sustained over time
because they cannot change,

00:43:03.000 --> 00:43:05.680
and they cannot go from
shackled to unshackled

00:43:05.680 --> 00:43:07.840
because they can't change.

00:43:07.840 --> 00:43:11.220
You can't take shackles off
of a person who can't change

00:43:11.220 --> 00:43:14.940
because taking off shackles
is to change them, got it?

00:43:14.940 --> 00:43:16.740
And if they're changing every millisecond,

00:43:16.740 --> 00:43:18.370
by the time you get your
hand on the shackles,

00:43:18.370 --> 00:43:20.548
it's somebody else's shackles.

00:43:20.548 --> 00:43:21.598
Okay, got it?

00:43:21.598 --> 00:43:25.206
,SNGA MA BZHIN DU SEMS CAN YANG,

00:43:25.206 --> 00:43:26.630
,MI 'CHING GROL BAR MI 'GYUR RO,

00:43:26.630 --> 00:43:28.596
SNGA MA BZHIN means, look,

00:43:28.596 --> 00:43:30.660
let's follow the same pattern as before.

00:43:30.660 --> 00:43:33.350
Now we established

00:43:33.350 --> 00:43:37.680
you can't take chains off
of Pachi's body and mind.

00:43:37.680 --> 00:43:38.630
- Why?

00:43:38.630 --> 00:43:41.380
- Because if they keep going
for any length of time,

00:43:41.380 --> 00:43:42.875
they can't change.

00:43:43.730 --> 00:43:46.430
And if they don't keep going
for any length of time,

00:43:46.430 --> 00:43:49.203
they're somebody else by the
time you get to the shackles.

00:43:50.070 --> 00:43:52.743
And if it applies to Seiji, sorry,

00:43:52.743 --> 00:43:56.750
Pachi's body and mind,
it also applies to Pachi.

00:43:56.750 --> 00:43:58.170
That's the second half of the verse.

00:43:58.170 --> 00:44:00.351
He's doing the same RIM PA, right?

00:44:00.351 --> 00:44:02.585
- What's that mean?
- [Woman] Steps.

00:44:02.585 --> 00:44:05.760
The same, the same,
there's parallel arguments.

00:44:05.760 --> 00:44:08.120
Let's treat Pachi's body and mind,

00:44:08.120 --> 00:44:09.660
and then let's treat Pachi.

00:44:09.660 --> 00:44:13.220
You cannot take chains off
of Pachi's body and mind

00:44:13.220 --> 00:44:15.030
because it has to be either
changing or unchanging,

00:44:15.030 --> 00:44:18.010
you can't take chains off
something, either one.

00:44:18.010 --> 00:44:21.630
And you can't take chains off of Pachi.

00:44:21.630 --> 00:44:25.850
Which is that aluminum Rebecca
who goes from life to life

00:44:25.850 --> 00:44:28.300
and drops bodies and minds
and takes new ones in

00:44:29.313 --> 00:44:31.510
because same problem.

00:44:31.510 --> 00:44:34.280
If he's changing, you don't have time

00:44:34.280 --> 00:44:37.440
to take his shackles off,
and if he's unchanging

00:44:37.440 --> 00:44:40.310
he can't get unshackled
when he used to be shackled

00:44:40.310 --> 00:44:42.560
because then he'd be changing, got it?

00:44:42.560 --> 00:44:46.200
It don't make sense to say
you can liberate a person.

00:44:46.200 --> 00:44:49.410
It don't make sense. Something's wrong.

00:44:49.410 --> 00:44:52.470
That's Nagarjuna's, the whole chapter is

00:44:52.470 --> 00:44:55.670
it don't make sense that
Pachi got into sansara,

00:44:55.670 --> 00:44:57.311
and it don't make sense that you can

00:44:57.311 --> 00:44:58.420
get Pachi out of sansara.

00:44:58.420 --> 00:45:00.860
Something's going on.

00:45:00.860 --> 00:45:04.070
There's a big problem here.

00:45:04.070 --> 00:45:08.350
Why does he go to liberation and shackles?

00:45:08.350 --> 00:45:10.530
I guess because we're so invested in it.

00:45:10.530 --> 00:45:13.531
We're reading his book because

00:45:13.531 --> 00:45:16.000
we want to change our life (laughs).

00:45:16.000 --> 00:45:18.630
That's why we're reading
the book in the first place.

00:45:18.630 --> 00:45:20.770
All right, here we go.

00:45:20.770 --> 00:45:22.990
Whoops, we finished the chapter. Yay!

00:45:22.990 --> 00:45:25.763
[students laughing]
So, okay, let's wrap up.

00:45:27.950 --> 00:45:31.743
If Pachi's the one moving
from lifetime to lifetime,

00:45:32.930 --> 00:45:36.150
then I don't know, he's unchanging because

00:45:36.150 --> 00:45:40.360
he's the unchanging Pachi who
picks up new bodies and minds

00:45:40.360 --> 00:45:43.900
and drops them, and goes and
picks up a new body and mind.

00:45:43.900 --> 00:45:47.470
That would imply that Pachi exists

00:45:47.470 --> 00:45:51.450
without his body and mind, which is crazy.

00:45:51.450 --> 00:45:54.780
Then if there is no Pachi,

00:45:54.780 --> 00:45:58.320
who holds his body and mind,

00:45:58.320 --> 00:46:00.830
and if Pachi's just his body and mind,

00:46:00.830 --> 00:46:03.220
then who goes to the next life?

00:46:03.220 --> 00:46:05.970
If this body and mind
died, then Pachi's gone

00:46:05.970 --> 00:46:08.130
because he's just his body and mind.

00:46:08.130 --> 00:46:10.055
- No, no, Pachi is the soul

00:46:10.055 --> 00:46:11.920
who holds onto his body and mind.

00:46:11.920 --> 00:46:14.090
- Well then he doesn't change.

00:46:14.090 --> 00:46:16.740
Then he's going to be in sansara forever.

00:46:16.740 --> 00:46:19.040
Cannot be liberated.

00:46:19.040 --> 00:46:21.753
Some kind of problem with Pachi.

00:46:22.660 --> 00:46:26.073
Alright, let's go to
the next chapter, yay!

